======================================================================================================================
DELIVERABLE 4 -- THE WRONG-RECOVERY LEDGER
======================================================================================================================
  PHANTOM = fitted component matching no true source at all.
  FAINT   = matches a real source that was not AVAILABLE. At 300 sources a
            bin, a random sky point lands within 0.15 rad of one of them
            0.815 of the time, so the faint column is
            mostly chance coincidence and is NOT a recovery.
  WRONG   = the V18 blend rate, (faint + phantom)/claims: the fraction of
            everything a ladder banks that is not a clean recovery.
  Null arm: the SAME sky, same noise draws, signal removed from BOTH blocks
  -- every component it claims is false. Certification columns carry the
  source-level scrambled null, run at every step of every ladder.

